{
 "about": "Highmark Foundry (caldera): the Bazookarp carrier's swim jumps over the lava, for the Bazookarp layout builder (karp-stages/). The lead's decision after review 6 (caldera LEAD-NOTES): a carrier swims its own ink (SPEC S21, 9.44 m/s), so its swim jumps over the lava are skill movement like everyone's; what a carrier may bypass is judged PER STAGE by the Bazookarp checker's shortcut probes (#7d) when Highmark's Bazookarp layout is built: that layout must place the Pond, the weirs and the Gate so no carrier jump saves over 20 m on the carrier field or skips a weir, with rails where it must (squids pass rails: a rail stops the kid's hop, not the swim). Its dash jumps are out (a carrier holds no sub). Source: tools/botlab/tests/lava-audit.js rule 44 with PAGE_ARGS full=1 at the fix-round-6 geometry (Organ L's crown, the stone corners): every plain swim crossing the kid makes saving > 10 m, tried again with the carrier's movement (actor.carry set: speeds x 0.8) from the same take-off, run-up and heading; 'gain' = the nav walk from the take-off node to where it landed minus the flight (the kid's own gain beside it). Both halves (x, z in world metres; Bravo's are the 180-degree turns). Review 6's probe-carry44 (at 4faa8d6f) found LOW 176 / 116 over 20 m / max 48.3, HIGH 92 / 23 / 29.5 retrying the older audit's list; this list is the corrected audit's at the new geometry.",
